/	FIXED POINT MATHEMATICAL PACKAGE

/	FIXED POINT DOUBLE-PRECISION MATHEMATICAL PACKAGE WITH INPUT AND OUTPUT
/	CONVERSION ROUTINES FOR VARIABLE FORMAT NUMBERS.

/	ALL INPUT/OUTPUT DONE VIA SIX-BIT ASCII STRINGS WITH ZERO HALF-WORD
/	DELIMITERS (TEXT STRINGS) OR 3 WORD MEMORY FORMAT.

/	INTERNAL ARITHMETIC CAN BE ACCOMPLISHED IN BINARY OR DECIMAL MODE.

/	DECIMAL ARITHMETIC WILL PRECISELY CALCULATE DECIMAL OPERANDS
/	(SUCH AS DECIMAL INPUT STRINGS).

/	BINARY ARITHMETIC WILL PRECISELY CALCULATE BINARY OPERANDS AND WILL
/	OPERATE FASTER, BUT CANNOT DEAL WITH DECIMAL OPERANDS PRECISELY DUE TO
/	THE INHERENT INABILITY TO REPRESENT DECIMAL VALUES IN BINARY.

/	ALL ERRORS ARE THE RESULT OF DECIMAL-BINARY CONVERSION.

/	ALSO INCLUDES A SIMPLE INTERPRETER FOR ALL FUNCTIONS.

/	(C)	1984, 1985, 1988	CHARLES LASNER ASSOCIATES.

/	LAST EDIT:	03-AUG-1988	13:00:00	CJL

/	ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS:

/	CHANGE "MTHFLD" ACCORDINGLY (DEFAULT IS 30).

/	CHANGE "MTHORG" ACCORDINGLY (DEFAULT IS 0200).

/	SET "EAE= 1" TO USE REAL PDP-8/E EAE HARDWARE (DEFAULT IS "EAE= 0"
/	TO INVOKE SIMULATION).

/	MAY BE ASSEMBLED WITH '/J' (OS/8 PAL8 '/F') SWITCH SET.

/	REQUIRES PDP-8/I PROCESSOR WITH EAE OR BETTER.

/	PDP-8/E OR BETTER PROCESSORS DO NOT REQUIRE EAE.

/	PDP-8/E EAE IS OPTIONALLY SUPPORTED.

/	CHANGE PARAMETERS HERE.

/	EAE=	0		/SIMULATE KE/8-E
/	MTHFLD=	30		/LOAD INTO FIELD THREE
/	MTHORG=	0200		/START AT 0200
/	FIXED POINT MATHEMATICAL PACKAGE DOCUMENTATION

/	INTRODUCTION TO FIXED POINT NUMBER SYSTEMS.

/	VARIOUS APPLICATIONS LEND THEMSELVES  TO  A  FIXED  NOTATION  SUCH AS COUNTING
/	MONEY TO THE NEAREST PENNY  (OR  TENTH  OF A PENNY).  THE SCALE OF THE DATA IS
/	KNOWN TO SOME ARBITRARY PRECISION WHICH MUST BE MAINTAINED.  MANY APPLICATIONS
/	WILL FAIL IF A FLOATING POINT SYSTEM  IS  CHOSEN, AS THE FLOATING POINT SYSTEM
/	WILL,  IN THE INTEREST OF MAINTAINING MAXIMUM ACCURACY,  OFTEN  ROUND  OFF  OR
/	OTHERWISE  LOSE  PRECISION.   FLOATING POINT SYSTEMS CANNOT MAINTAIN  ACCURACY
/	BEYOND A CERTAIN NUMBER OF BITS, THOUGH THEY SOMETIMES APPEAR TO (THE INTERNAL
/	SCALE  MERELY  SHIFTED  TO  MAINTAIN  THE MOST SIGNIFICANT BITS OF THE  NUMBER
/	CURRENTLY STORED) AND WILL ALWAYS HAVE "PLAUSIBLE," THOUGH INACCURATE RESULTS.
/	OFTEN WHAT IS NEEDED (SUCH AS IN MONETARY CALCULATIONS) IS A SYSTEM CAPABLE OF
/	MAINTAINING  FULL  ACCURACY COUPLED  WITH  A  MECHANISM  TO  DETECT  UNDERFLOW
/	(TRUNCATION) AND OVERFLOW.  UNDERFLOW  OCCURS  WHEN A (PORTION OF A) NUMBER IS
/	TOO SMALL TO BE REPRESENTED IN  THE CURRENT SCALE (SUCH AS FRACTIONS OF A CENT
/	IN THE MONEY EXAMPLE TO THE NEAREST PENNY).  NUMBERS UNDERFLOW AND BECOME ZERO
/	UNITS  OF THE CURRENT SCALE, OR ARE TRUNCATED  TO  THE  NEAREST  UNIT  OF  THE
/	PREVAILING SCALE.  SEVERAL EXAMPLES ARE:

/	$      10.00999 =>      $      10.00    TRUNCATION TO NEAREST CENT
/	$       0.00999 =>      $       0.00    TRUNCATION TO ZERO CENTS

/	TRUNCATION INDICATES THE  IMPOSSIBILITY  OF  REPRESENTING  THE  NUMBER  IN THE
/	CURRENT SCALE.  EITHER  THE  SCALE  WAS CHOSEN WRONG, OR THE NUMBER REPRESENTS
/	FALSE INFORMATION.  IN EITHER  CASE,  THE  SYSTEM  SHOULD  FLAG  THIS ERROR IN
/	USAGE.

/	OVERFLOW OCCURS WHEN THE MAXIMUM VALUE POSSIBLE WITHIN THE SYSTEM IS EXCEEDED.
/	UNLIKE FLOATING POINT SYSTEMS WHICH WOULD MERELY  REDEFINE  THE  SCALE  OF THE
/	NUMBER (PERHAPS RETAINING ONLY THE HIGHEST DIGITS), FIXED  POINT  SYSTEMS WILL
/	FLAG THE ERROR, SINCE ABSOLUTE ACCURACY IS ONLY POSSIBLE  WHERE ALL DIGITS ARE
/	RETAINED.  IT IS ALSO POSSIBLE TO HAVE TRUNCATION AND OVERFLOW SIMULTANEOUSLY.
/	SEVERAL EXAMPLES ARE:

/	$ 1234567.      =>      $       ?.??    TOO MANY DIGITS WILL OVERFLOW
/	$  123456.999   =>      $  123456.99    TRUNCATION TO NEAREST CENT
/	$ 9999999.999   =>      $       ?.??    OVERFLOW AND TRUNCATION

/	THERE  ARE CIRCUMSTANCES WHERE A NUMBER IMPLIES PRECISION VIA  TRAILING  ZEROS
/	WHICH  ALLOWS  ACCURATE  REPRESENTATION  IN  THE  CURRENT  SCALE, ALTHOUGH THE
/	TRAILING  ZEROS  ARE  NOT  RETAINED.  THIS IS DEFINED AS A  "SOFT"  TRUNCATION
/	ERROR, AS A WARNING TO THE USER THAT THE TRAILING ZEROS WERE  DROPPED.    THIS
/	CAN MERELY BE A REMOVAL OF EXTRANEOUS INFORMATION (USERS SOMETIMES TYPE IN TOO
/	MANY TRAILING  ZEROS), OR CAN REPRESENT AN INCOMPATIBILITY OF SCALE AND NUMBER
/	WHERE NORMAL TRUNCATION  WAS  AVOIDED  SIMPLY BECAUSE THE TRAILING DIGITS WERE
/	ZERO.  HAD THEY BEEN NON-ZERO, TRUNCATION DEFINITELY WOULD HAVE OCCURRED.  THE
/	SYSTEM SHOULD FLAG THIS SITUATION AS WELL AT THE SYSTEM DESIGNER'S OPTION.

/	ALL  OF  THE  ABOVE  IDEAS  ARE EMBODIED WITHIN THIS  PACKAGE.    VIA  SEVERAL
/	OPERATING MODES, COMPLETE AND ACCURATE CALCULATIONS CAN BE PERFORMED ON  FIXED
/	POINT NUMBERS WITH A WIDE RANGE OF SCALES TO CHOOSE FROM.
/	ASSEMBLY DEFINITIONS, ETC.
	XLIST	OFF
	IFNDEF	OFF	<OFF=	1>
	IFNDEF	ON	<ON=	0>

	IFNDEF	EAE	<EAE=	0>	/SIMULATE KE-8/E
	IFNDEF	MTHFLD	<MTHFLD=30>	/ASSEMBLY FIELD
	IFNDEF	MTHORG	<MTHORG=0200>	/ASSEMBLY ORIGIN
	XLIST	ON

/	COMMON EAE DEFINITIONS (MUST BE FUNCTIONAL EVEN IF SIMULATING).

	CAM=	7621			/CLEAR AC, MQ
	MQA=	7501			/OR MQ INTO AC
	MQL=	7421			/LOAD AC INTO MQ, CLEAR AC
	SWP=	7521			/SWAP AC, MQ

/	ADDITIONAL EAE DEFINITIONS FOR USE WITH REAL KE-8/E HARDWARE.

	DAD=	7443			/DOUBLE-PRECISION ADD
	DCM=	7575			/DOUBLE-PRECISION TWO'S COMPLEMENT
	DLD=	7663			/DOUBLE-PRECISION LOAD
	DST=	7445			/DOUBLE-PRECISION STORE
	DVI=	7407			/DIVIDE
	LSR=	7417			/LOGICAL SHIFT RIGHT
	MUY=	7405			/MULTIPLY
	NMI=	7411			/NORMALIZE
	SCA=	7441			/STEP COUNTER TO AC
	SHL=	7413			/SHIFT LEFT
	SWAB=	7431			/FORCE MODE "B" EAE

/	PACKAGE OPCODE DEFINITIONS (**** MEANS INTERPRETER ONLY).

	ADD=	0001			/ADD OPERAND TO MAC
	BINARY=	0010			/**** SETUP BINARY ARITHMETIC (0=DECIMAL)
	CLEAR=	0000			/CLEAR MAC
	DIV=	0004			/DIVIDE MAC BY OPERAND
	EXIT=	4000			/**** EXIT INTERPRETER
	FUNCTIO=0005			/PERFORM SPECIFIED FUNCTION ON MAC
	IDIV=	0014			/**** DIVIDE OPERAND BY MAC
	ISUB=	0012			/**** SUBTRACT MAC FROM OPERAND
	MACOUT=	0006			/OUTPUT MAC INTO OPERAND
	MEMODE=	0001			/OPERANDS IN MEMORY (0=TEXT STRINGS)
	MUL=	0003			/MULTIPLY MAC BY OPERAND
	NEGATE=	0000			/NEGATE MAC
	SAVE=	0002			/**** SETUP OPERAND "DON'T CLEAR MAC" BIT
					/(NOT VALID IF SCALE FACTOR CHANGES)
	SCALE=	0400			/**** SETUP OPERAND INPUT SCALE FACTOR
	SETFLD=	0010			/**** SETUP FIELD OF OPERANDS
	SETFORM=0013			/**** SETUP OUTPUT FORMAT
	SETOUT=	0011			/**** SETUP OUTPUT SPECIAL FUNCTION BITS
	SETUP=	0007			/SETUP INTERNAL SCALE AND CLEAR MAC
	SFTIGNO=0040			/**** SETUP OPERAND "IGNORE SOFT
					/TRUNCATION ERRORS" BIT
	SQROOT=	7777			/TAKE SQUARE ROOT OF MAC
	SQUARE=	0001			/SQUARE MAC
	STORE=	0006			/OUTPUT MAC INTO OPERAND
	SUB=	0002			/SUBTRACT OPERAND FROM MAC
	TRIGNOR=0100			/**** SETUP OPERAND "IGNORE TRUNCATION
					/ERRORS" BIT
/	OPERATE DEFINITIONS.

	NL0001=	CLA IAC			/LOAD AC WITH 0001
	NL0002=	CLA CLL CML RTL		/LOAD AC WITH 0002
	NL0004=	CLA CLL IAC RTL		/LOAD AC WITH 0004
	NL2000=	CLA CLL CML RTR		/LOAD AC WITH 2000
	NL3777=	CLA CLL CMA RAR		/LOAD AC WITH 3777
	NL4000=	CLA CLL CML RAR		/LOAD AC WITH 4000
	NL7775=	CLA CLL CMA RTL		/LOAD AC WITH 7775
	NL7776=	CLA CLL CMA RAL		/LOAD AC WITH 7776
	NL7777=	CLA CMA			/LOAD AC WITH 7777

/	VERSION DEFINITIONS.

	REVISIO="D			/REVISION LETTER
	VERSION="1			/VERSION NUMBER
/	MAIN ENTRY POINT FOR MATH PACKAGE.

/	CALLING SEQUENCE:

/	CDF	MYFLD			/SET CALLING FIELD
/	CIF	MTHFLD			/GOTO ROUTINE FIELD
/	TAD	(SPECIAL)		/OPTIONAL VALUE FOR CERTAIN CALLS, SEE BELOW
/	JMS I	(MTHPAK)		/CALL PACKAGE
/	SPECIAL^100+BUFFLD^10+OPCODE	/BUFFER FIELD, OPCODE, SPECIAL BITS, SEE BELOW
/	BUFFER				/12-BIT BUFFER ADDRESS
/	ERROR				/ERROR RETURN, SEE BELOW
/	GOOD				/RETURNS HERE WITH CLEAR AC IF NO ERRORS

/	SPECIAL OPTIONS IN AC:

/	SETUP OPCODE ONLY:

/	IF AC[0]=1	THEN DON'T CLEAR MAC (NOT VALID IF CHANGING SCALE FACTOR).

/	IF AC[0]=0	THEN CLEAR MAC.

/	IF AC[1]=1	THEN SET MEMORY OPERAND FORMAT (3 WORD).

/	IF AC[1]=0	THEN SET TEXT OPERAND FORMAT (VARIABLE LENGTH STRINGS).

/	IF AC[3]=1	THEN IGNORE TRUNCATION ERRORS.

/	IF AC[3]=0	THEN ALLOW TRUNCATION ERRORS.

/	IF AC[4]=1	THEN IGNORE SOFT TRUNCATION ERRORS.

/	IF AC[4]=0	THEN ALLOW SOFT TRUNCATION ERRORS.

/	IF AC[11]=1	THEN INTERNAL ARITHMETIC IS DONE IN BINARY MODE.

/	IF AC[11]=0	THEN INTERNAL ARITHMETIC IS DONE IN DECIMAL.

/	SUBTRACT OPCODE ONLY:

/	IF AC[0-11]=	7777 THEN DO AN INVERSE SUBTRACT (MAC=	OPERAND-MAC).

/	DIVIDE OPCODE ONLY:

/	IF AC[0-11]=	7777 THEN DO AN INVERSE DIVIDE (MAC=	OPERAND/MAC).

/	FUNCTION OPCODE ONLY:

/	AC[0-11]	OFFSET INTO FUNCTION TABLE.
/	OUTPUT OPCODE ONLY:

/	AC[0-3]:	SIGNED POWER OF TEN USED TO REPRESENT OUTPUT. POSITIVE
/			VALUES CREATE INTEGER OUTPUT WITHOUT A DECIMAL POINT.

/	AC[4-7]:	COUNT OF ADDITIONAL BLANKS PADDING THE OUTPUT FIELD
/			ON THE RIGHT.

/	AC[8-11]:	TOTAL FIELD WIDTH INCLUDING LEADING BLANKS, OPTIONAL
/			SIGN CHARACTER, DECIMAL POINT. DOES NOT INCLUDE WIDTH
/			OF OPTIONAL BLANKS PADDING THE OUTPUT FIELD ON THE RIGHT.

/	SPECIAL OPTIONS IN FIRST ARGUMENT WORD:

/	SETUP OPCODE ONLY:

/	BIT[0-3]:	SCALE FACTOR - SIGNED POWER OF TEN USED FOR THE INTERNAL
/			REPRESENTATION OF NUMBERS WHEN IN DECIMAL MODE. THIS
/			VALUE WILL BE USED TO APPROXIMATE THE SIGNED POWER OF TWO
/			CORRESPONDINGLY USED IN BINARY MODE.

/	OUTPUT OPCODE ONLY:

/	BIT[0]=	1	SUPPRESS LEADING CHARACTER ON POSITIVE OUTPUT (IGNORE BIT[1]).

/	BIT[0]=	0	USE BIT[1] TO DETERMINE LEADING CHARACTER ON POSITIVE OUTPUT

/	BIT[1]=	1	USE "+" ON POSITIVE OUTPUT.

/	BIT[1]=	0	USE " " ON POSITIVE OUTPUT.

/	BIT[2]=	1	USE LEADING SIGN CHARACTER ON LEFT.

/	BIT[2]=	0	USE SIGN CHARACTER JUST LEFT OF DIGITS.

/	BIT[3]=	1	DON'T USE LEADING ZERO ON FRACTIONAL OUTPUT.

/	BIT[3]=	0	USE LEADING ZERO ON FRACTIONAL OUTPUT.
/	ERROR INDICATORS IN AC:

/	AC[0]=	1	OPERATION OVERFLOWED; OPERATION ABORTED AND RESULTS ARE GARBAGE.

/	AC[1]=	1	INPUT OPERAND HAS BAD CHARACTERS; MATH AC STILL VALID.

/	AC[3]=	1	TRUNCATION ERROR; PRECISION LOST BUT OTHERWISE VALID.

/	AC[4]=	1	SOFT TRUNCATION ERROR; TRAILING ZEROES PAST DECIMAL POINT
/			WERE TRUNCATED, BUT PRECISION IS MAINTAINED.
/			INDICATES POSSIBLE INCORRECT SETUP OF INPUT SCALE.

/	AC[5]=	1	OUTPUT CONVERSION ERROR; OUTPUT CANNOT BE CONVERTED TO
/			REQUESTED FORMAT (CAUSES OVERFLOW IN CONVERSION). MATH AC
/			STILL VALID.

/	AC[9]=	1	OUTPUT CONVERSION ERROR. OUTPUT WIDTH GREATER THAN
/			REQUESTED FIELD WIDTH OR OVERFLOW WHILE ATTEMPTING TO
/			CONVERT ORIGINAL MATH AC TO DESIRED SCALE. MATH AC STILL VALID.

/	AC[10]=	1	INPUT OPERAND OVERFLOWED; MATH AC STILL VALID.

/	AC=	7777	INVALID FUNCTION TYPE.

/	SQUARE ROOT FUNCTION ONLY:

/	AC[1]=	1	ABS(MAC) IS NOT POSITIVE.

/	AC[9]=	1	MAC WAS NEGATIVE; SQUARE ROOT OF ABSOLUTE VALUE TAKEN.
/	THE CODE STARTS HERE.

	FIELD	MTHFLD%10	/SETUP FIELD

	*MTHORG			/SETUP ORIGIN

MTHPAK,	VERSION^100+REVISION-300/MATH PACKAGE ENTRY POINT
	DCA	ACOPTIONS	/SAVE POSSIBLE AC OPTION BITS
	RDF			/GET CALLING FIELD
	TAD	(CIF CDF)	/MAKE INTO CIF CDF RETURN INSTRUCTION
	DCA	MTHPXT		/STORE FOR EXIT LATER
	TAD I	MTHPAK		/GET OPCODE WORD
	DCA	OPCODE		/STASH IT
	ISZ	MTHPAK		/BUMP TO NEXT
	TAD I	MTHPAK		/GET BUFFER ADDRESS
	DCA	ADDRESS		/STASH IT
	ISZ	MTHPAK		/BUMP PAST BUFFER ADDRESS
	CDF	MTHFLD		/GOTO OUR FIELD
	SWAB			/ENSURE MODE "B"
	NOP			/IN CASE OF PDP-8/I
	CAM			/CLEAN UP
	DCA	MFLAGS		/CLEAR INPUT ERROR FLAGS
	TAD	OPCODE		/GET OPCODE WORD
	AND	(7)		/JUST OPCODE BITS
	TAD	(JMP I	OPTABLE)/MAKE INTO CORRECT JUMP
	DCA	GPTEMP		/STORE IN-LINE
GPTEMP,	.-.			/WILL BE JMP I OPTABLE+X

/	OPCODE DISPATCH TABLE.

OPTABLE,MCLEAR			/0=	CLEAR MAC
	MADD			/1=	ADD OPERAND TO MAC
	MSUB			/2=	SUBTRACT OPERAND FROM MAC
	MMUL			/3=	MULTIPLY MAC BY OPERAND
	MDIV			/4=	DIVIDE MAC BY OPERAND
	MFUN			/5=	PERFORM FUNCTION ON MAC
	MOUTPUT			/6=	CONVERT MAC TO ASCII STRING (OR STORAGE)
	MSETUP			/7=	SETUP INTERNAL SCALE, CLEAR MAC

/	FUNCTION CALL.

MFUN,	TAD	ACOPTIONS	/GET PASSED VALUE
	TAD	(20)		/OFFSET IT
	AND	(7740)		/CHECK FOR BAD VALUES
	SZA CLA			/SKIP IF OK
	JMP	MDUMMY		/ELSE COMPLAIN
	TAD	(MFUNTBL+20)	/GET TABLE POINTER
	TAD	ACOPTIONS	/OFFSET TO CALLER'S CHOICE
	DCA	GPTEMP		/STASH THE POINTER
	TAD I	GPTEMP		/GET THE ROUTINE ADDRESS
	DCA	GPTEMP		/STASH IT
	JMP I	GPTEMP		/GO THERE
/	ERROR FUNCTION FOR BAD FUNCTION CALLS.

MDUMMY,	NL7777			/SET ERROR VALUE
	JMP	MTHPXT		/TAKE FAILURE RETURN

/	COMES HERE WHEN DONE. AC BITS ON INDICATE VARIOUS ERRORS.

MDONE,	TAD	MFLAGS		/ADD ON INPUT ERROR FLAGS
MDONE2,	AND	MMASK		/REMOVE MASKED BITS
	SNA			/SKIP IF ANY ERRORS
	ISZ	MTHPAK		/BUMP TO GOOD RETURN IF NO ERRORS
MTHPXT,	.-.			/WILL BE CIF CDF RETURN FIELD
	JMP I	MTHPAK		/RETURN TO CALLER

MOUTPUT,TAD	IOSW		/GET MODE SWITCH
	SMA CLA			/SKIP IF MEMORY MODE
	JMP I	(MSTORE)	/ELSE USE TEXT STRING
	TAD	OPCODE		/GET OPCODE WORD
	AND	(70)		/JUST FIELD BITS
	TAD	(CDF)		/TURN INTO CDF USER FIELD
	DCA	.+1		/STORE IN-LINE
	.-.			/AND EXECUTE
	TAD	MADJST		/GET EXPONENT
	DCA I	ADDRESS		/STORE IT
	ISZ	ADDRESS		/BUMP TO NEXT
	TAD	MACHI		/GET HIGH-ORDER MANTISSA
	DCA I	ADDRESS		/STORE IT
	ISZ	ADDRESS		/BUMP TO NEXT
	TAD	MACLO		/GET LOW-ORDER MANTISSA
	DCA I	ADDRESS		/STORE IT
	JMP	MDONE		/FINISH IT THERE
INSETUP,.-.			/INPUT SETUP ROUTINE
	NL4000			/SETUP MASK
	AND	IOSW		/GET MODE SWITCH
	CLL RAL			/MOVE TO LINK
	TAD	OPCODE		/GET OPCODE WORD
	AND	(70)		/JUST FIELD BITS
	TAD	(CDF)		/FORM CDF INSTRUCTION
	SNL			/BINARY MODE?
	JMP	INTEXT		/NO, USE TEXT MODE
	DCA	.+1		/STORE IN-LINE
	.-.			/AND EXECUTE IT
	TAD I	ADDRESS		/GET A WORD
	DCA	DPCNT		/SAVE AS EXPONEXT
	ISZ	ADDRESS		/BUMP TO NEXT
	TAD I	ADDRESS		/GET NEXT WORD
	DCA	HI		/STORE AS HIGH-ORDER MANTISSA
	ISZ	ADDRESS		/BUMP TO NEXT
	TAD I	ADDRESS		/GET NEXT WORD
	DCA	LO		/STORE AS LOW-ORDER MANTISSA
	CDF	MTHFLD		/RESTORE OUR FIELD
	JMP I	(MEMENT)	/CONTINUE THERE

INTEXT,	DCA I	(GETCDF)	/STORE FOR GET HALF ROUTINE
	DCA I	(GETNDX)	/CLEAR INPUT INDEX
	TAD	ADDRESS		/GET ADDRESS ARGUMENT
	DCA I	(GETBASE)	/STORE AS BUFFER BASE
	JMP I	INSETUP		/RETURN
ACOPTIO,.-.			/OPTIONS PASSED IN AC
ADDRESS,.-.			/OPERAND ADDRESS
BINDECM,.-.			/BINARY/DECIMAL MODE SWITCH
DPCNT,	.-.			/INPUT SCALE FACTOR
IOSW,	.-.			/BINARY/TEXT SWITCH
MADJST,	.-.			/MAC SCALE FACTOR
MFLAGS,	.-.			/NON-FATAL INPUT ERROR FLAGS
OPCODE,	.-.			/OPCODE WORD

/	MATH ACCUMULATOR.

	MAC=	.		/MATH AC

MACLO,	.-.			/MAC - LOW-ORDER
MACHI,	.-.			/MAC - HIGH-ORDER

/	BUFFER.

	OPERAND=.		/OPERAND

LO,	.-.			/BUFFER - LOW-ORDER
HI,	.-.			/BUFFER - HIGH-ORDER
HIGHER,	.-.			/ADDITIONAL REGISTERS
HIGHEST,.-.			/FOR MULTIPLY OPERATIONS

/	ERROR MASK.

MMASK,	7777			/CAN BE ADJUSTED TO IGNORE ERRORS.

	PAGE
	XLIST	OFF
	IFZERO	EAE	<
	XLIST	ON
/	DEFINITIONS FOR THIS PAGE.

	DAD=	JMS I	(XDAD)	/DOUBLE-PRECISION ADD
	DCM=	JMS I	(XDCM)	/DOUBLE-PRECISION TWO'S COMPLEMENT
	DLD=	JMS I	(XDLD)	/DOUBLE-PRECISION LOAD
	DST=	JMS I	(XDST)	/DOUBLE-PRECISION STORE

	XLIST	OFF	>
	XLIST	ON
/	ADDITION ROUTINE.

MADD,	JMS	ADDSUB		/CALL COMMON ROUTINE
	DCA I	(ACOPTIONS)	/PREVENT INVERSION
MSUBIN,	NL4000			/SET SIGN MASK
	AND I	(MACHI)		/GET SIGN BIT OF MAC
	TAD I	(HI)		/COMPARE TO SIGN BIT OF OPERAND
	DCA	OVTEST		/SAVE FOR COMPARISON LATER
	DLD;	MAC		/LOAD MAC
	DAD;	OPERAND		/ADD ON OPERAND
	DCA	MADTMP		/SAVE HIGH-ORDER FOR NOW
	TAD	OVTEST		/GET ORIGINAL SIGNS
	SPA CLA			/SKIP IF PROBLEMATIC
	JMP	ARITHOK		/JUMP IF NOT
	NL4000			/SET SIGN MASK
	AND I	(MACHI)		/GET SIGN OF RESULT
	TAD I	(HI)		/COMPARE TO SIGN BIT OF OPERAND
	SMA CLA			/SKIP IF BAD
	JMP	ARITHOK		/JUMP IF OK
MOVFL,	NL4000			/SET ERROR BIT
	JMP I	(MDONE2)	/EXIT THERE

ARITHOK,TAD	MADTMP		/RESTORE HIGH-ORDER RESULT
	ISZ I	(ACOPTIONS)	/SHOULD WE INVERT?
	SKP			/NO, NORMAL CASE
MNEGIN,	DCM			/YES, -(MAC-OPERAND)= OPERAND-MAC
MOK,	DST;	MAC		/STORE IN MAC
	CAM			/CLEAN UP
	JMP I	(MDONE)		/RETURN TO CALLER

/	SUBTRACTION ROUTINE.

MSUB,	JMS	ADDSUB		/CALL COMMON ROUTINE
	DLD;	OPERAND		/LOAD THE OPERAND
	DCM			/FORM -OPERAND
	DST;	OPERAND		/STORE IT BACK
	JMP	MSUBIN		/CONTINUE THERE

/	NEGATION ROUTINE.

MNEG,	DLD;	MAC		/GET MAC
	JMP	MNEGIN		/CONTINUE THERE
/	SQUARE FUNCTION.

MSQR,	TAD I	(MADJST)	/GET MAC SCALE
	DCA I	(DPCNT)		/USE FOR OPERAND
	DLD;	MAC		/GET MAC
	DST;	OPERAND		/USE AS OPERAND
	NL7777			/SETUP THE
	DCA I	(MSIGN)		/SIGN SWITCH
	JMP I	(MSQRENTRY)	/CONTINUE THERE

/	SHIFT "LO, HI, HIGHER, HIGHEST" TO THE LEFT ROUTINE.

SHL48,	.-.			/SHIFT LEFT ROUTINE
	DCA	SHFTCNT		/SAVE PASSED NEGATIVE SHIFT COUNT
SHLOOP,	TAD	SHFTCNT		/GET CURRENT VALUE
	TAD	(14)		/CAN WE SHIFT IT A WORD AT A TIME?
	SMA SZA			/SKIP IF SO
	JMP	SMALLSHIFT	/JUMP IF NOT
	DCA	SHFTCNT		/STORE REMAINING COUNT
	TAD I	(HIGHER)	/GET NEXT TO LAST
	DCA I	(HIGHEST)	/MAKE IT THE LAST
	TAD I	(HI)		/GET SECOND
	DCA I	(HIGHER)	/MAKE IT NEXT TO LAST
	TAD I	(LO)		/GET LOWEST
	DCA I	(HI)		/MAKE IT SECOND
	DCA I	(LO)		/CLEAR LOWEST
	JMP	SHLOOP		/TRY AGAIN

SMALLSH,TAD	(-14)		/RESET TO NEGATIVE COUNT
	SMA			/SKIP IF ANY LEFT TO DO
	JMP I	SHL48		/RETURN IF NOT
	DCA	SHFTCNT		/SAVE CORRECTED COUNT
	JMS	SHFL48		/MOVE UP ONE BIT
	ISZ	SHFTCNT		/DONE ENOUGH?
	JMP	.-2		/NO, KEEP GOING
	JMP I	SHL48		/YES, RETURN

/	SHIFT "LO, HI, HIGHER, HIGHEST" LEFT ONE BIT ROUTINE.

SHFL48,	.-.			/SHIFT LEFT ONE BIT ROUTINE
	TAD I	(LO)		/GET LOWEST
	CLL RAL			/MOVE UP ONE
	DCA I	(LO)		/STORE IT BACK
	TAD I	(HI)		/GET NEXT
	RAL			/MOVE UP ONE
	DCA I	(HI)		/STORE IT BACK
	TAD I	(HIGHER)	/GET NEXT
	RAL			/MOVE UP ONE
	DCA I	(HIGHER)	/STORE IT BACK
	TAD I	(HIGHEST)	/GET LAST
	RAL			/MOVE UP ONE
	DCA I	(HIGHEST)	/STORE IT BACK
